WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.660
2.8 million extra corn hectares raised nitrate flowing into the Gulf. This is unintended consequences

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:12.300
episode 146. In the spring of 2008, farmers across Iowa and Illinois prepared fields

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:17.500
for record corn plantings. Congress had passed the Energy Independence and Security Act the

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:22.820
previous December. Policy makers had meant the expanded renewable fuel standard to cut oil

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:27.760
imports and to lower tailpipe emissions. The route they chose was blending more corn

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:33.080
ethanol into gasoline. The same policy increased synthetic nitrogen applications on Midwest

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:38.320
cropland. Additional nitrate loads moved down the Mississippi River toward the Gulf of Mexico.

00:00:39.416 --> 00:00:45.396
President George W. Bush signed the Energy Independence and Security Act on December 19, 2007.

00:00:46.156 --> 00:00:51.656
Both houses of Congress had approved the law with bipartisan support. Title 2 of the law expanded

00:00:51.656 --> 00:00:57.916
the renewable fuel standard that Congress had created in 2005. The new statute set rising annual

00:00:57.916 --> 00:01:04.256
volume requirements. Those requirements reached 36 billion gallons of renewable fuel by 2022.

00:01:05.116 --> 00:01:10.416
At the time, crude oil prices were high in volatile. The United States depended on imported

00:01:10.416 --> 00:01:16.756
petroleum. Greenhouse gas emissions from transportation were a standing concern. Against that background,

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:22.496
greater domestic bio-fuel production looked like a practical step. Law makers and agency staff

00:01:22.496 --> 00:01:28.496
at the Environmental Protection Agency, the EPA, saw Cornstarch ethanol as a fuel already

00:01:28.496 --> 00:01:33.636
in commercial use. Cornstarch ethanol could scale quickly without new engine technology.

00:01:34.176 --> 00:01:38.576
The policy therefore rewarded increased corn production as the most direct route to the

00:01:38.576 --> 00:01:46.656
statutory targets. Between 2005 and 2007, oil repeatedly exceeded $70 per barrel. Supply

00:01:46.656 --> 00:01:51.556
disruptions in the Middle East were still fresh and legislative memory, substituting a portion

00:01:51.556 --> 00:01:56.176
of gasoline demand with a domestically grown liquid fuel lined up with security goals.

00:01:56.736 --> 00:02:01.536
The same substitution lined up with environmental goals many legislators had already endorsed

00:02:01.536 --> 00:02:06.696
in the earlier Energy Policy Act. The people writing the volumes were not guessing in the dark

00:02:06.696 --> 00:02:12.036
about engines or refineries. They were extending a fuel pathway the country already knew how to make.

00:02:13.024 --> 00:02:18.764
The statute took effect immediately. The EPA began issuing annual renewable volume obligations.

00:02:18.764 --> 00:02:23.544
Those obligations required refiners to blend specified quantities of ethanol.

00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:31.184
Corn prices rose roughly 30% between 2008 and 2016 as demand for ethanol feedstock grew.

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:36.764
In the first years after enactment, ethanol production capacity expanded rapidly in the Midwest.

00:02:37.444 --> 00:02:41.864
By 2010, the industry was on track to meet the laws intermediate targets.

00:02:42.724 --> 00:02:48.284
Early reports from the Department of Agriculture noted higher farm incomes and greater domestic fuel output.

00:02:48.284 --> 00:02:53.464
it. For farm communities watching those reports, the policy looked like it was doing what

00:02:53.464 --> 00:02:59.824
Congress had asked. A few hydrologists warned otherwise. Researchers later cited in a 2008

00:02:59.824 --> 00:03:05.044
paper by Donner and Kucharik, published in the proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences,

00:03:05.724 --> 00:03:12.264
PNAS, said meeting the full ethanol volumes would require more corn acreage. More corn acreage

00:03:12.264 --> 00:03:17.284
would require more fertilizer. Those cautions received limited attention during the rollout.

00:03:17.284 --> 00:03:22.744
Refiners met their obligations by purchasing renewable identification numbers tied to each

00:03:22.744 --> 00:03:23.664
gallon of ethanol.

00:03:24.104 --> 00:03:26.204
That purchase created a liquid market.

00:03:26.644 --> 00:03:30.824
The market transmitted statutory demand directly into the corn futures price.

00:03:31.424 --> 00:03:36.224
Because the volume schedule increased each year, the price signal stayed consistent rather

00:03:36.224 --> 00:03:36.984
than temporary.

00:03:37.544 --> 00:03:40.864
A farmer planning the next season was not looking at a one-year spike.

00:03:41.424 --> 00:03:44.124
The farmer was looking at a schedule written to keep rising.

00:03:44.124 --> 00:03:51.772
Larkin colleagues in a PNAS paper in 2022 combined econometric land use models with

00:03:51.772 --> 00:03:57.012
biophysical data. The study found that the renewable fuel standard increased United States

00:03:57.012 --> 00:04:02.012
corn acreage by the amount named at the top of this episode and increased total crop

00:04:02.012 --> 00:04:09.912
land by 2.1 million hectares between 2008 and 2016. The same study estimated that nationwide

00:04:09.912 --> 00:04:15.432
synthetic nitrogen fertilizer use rose 7.5 percent. Nitrate leaching from

00:04:15.432 --> 00:04:20.832
agricultural soils increased 5.3 percent. Most of the additional corn was grown

00:04:20.832 --> 00:04:25.312
in the Mississippi River Basin. A larger share of that reactive nitrogen moved

00:04:25.312 --> 00:04:30.952
downstream. Donner and Cucharix earlier PNAS modeling had projected a further rise.

00:04:31.552 --> 00:04:35.732
Satisfying the ethanol mandates that modeling said would raise dissolved

00:04:35.732 --> 00:04:41.572
inorganic nitrogen export by the Mississippi-Achafalaya system between 10 and 34%.

00:04:41.572 --> 00:04:45.312
The extra nitrate reached the northern Gulf of Mexico each summer.

00:04:45.992 --> 00:04:48.192
There, the nitrate fueled algal blooms.

00:04:48.612 --> 00:04:52.172
The subsequent decay of those blooms depleted oxygen in bottom waters.

00:04:52.752 --> 00:04:56.452
The seasonal hypoxic area was already large before 2007.

00:04:57.072 --> 00:05:01.792
The area therefore faced additional nutrient pressure that made reduction targets harder to reach.

00:05:01.792 --> 00:05:07.152
Farmers responded to higher corn prices by planting continuous corn rather than rotating

00:05:07.152 --> 00:05:12.552
with soybeans. That shift further raised nitrogen requirements. Equipment dealers and

00:05:12.552 --> 00:05:18.092
fertilizer suppliers adjusted inventories accordingly. Those inventory choices locked in the higher

00:05:18.092 --> 00:05:23.032
application rates for multiple seasons. The policy's price signal operated nationwide.

00:05:23.652 --> 00:05:28.612
Even regions outside the traditional corn belt saw expanded corn plantings and associated

00:05:28.612 --> 00:05:33.352
fertiliser use. One consequence of the continuous corn shift is that soybean

00:05:33.352 --> 00:05:38.332
nitrogen credits disappear. A legume leaves nitrogen in the soil for the next crop.

00:05:38.992 --> 00:05:43.152
After soybeans, a following corn crop can often take a reduced nitrogen rate.

00:05:43.632 --> 00:05:48.332
Each additional hectare and continuous corn receives a full recommended nitrogen rate instead.

00:05:48.932 --> 00:05:52.872
That full rate amplified the modeled national increase in reactive nitrogen.

00:05:53.532 --> 00:05:57.512
The Mississippi basin drains roughly 40% of United States crop land.

00:05:57.512 --> 00:06:02.572
even modest percentage rises in application translate into thousands of additional tons

00:06:02.572 --> 00:06:04.652
of nitrogen reaching the river each year.

00:06:05.172 --> 00:06:08.272
Picture the chain as a set of doors that all opened the same way.

00:06:08.772 --> 00:06:10.812
A gallon target became a blending duty.

00:06:11.292 --> 00:06:13.372
A blending duty became a tradable credit.

00:06:13.832 --> 00:06:15.752
A tradable credit became a corn price.

00:06:16.292 --> 00:06:18.232
A corn price became a planting decision.

00:06:18.692 --> 00:06:23.312
A planting decision became fertilizer on a field that drains eventually to a summer dead

00:06:23.312 --> 00:06:23.652
zone.

00:06:23.652 --> 00:06:27.312
None of those doors required a person to intend harm to the Gulf.

00:06:27.872 --> 00:06:30.932
Each door only required someone to meet the metric in front of them.

00:06:31.825 --> 00:06:36.405
By the mid-2010s, the modeled water quality effects had entered regulatory discussions.

00:06:37.005 --> 00:06:39.525
The statutory volume mandates remained in place.

00:06:40.165 --> 00:06:42.665
The EPA continued to adjust annual standards.

00:06:43.205 --> 00:06:46.585
The agency did not alter the underlying corn ethanol pathway.

00:06:47.145 --> 00:06:52.085
Industry groups disputed the magnitude of the nitrogen increases reported by Lark and colleagues.

00:06:52.085 --> 00:06:56.945
Those groups argued that yield improvements and improved nutrient management had offset

00:06:56.945 --> 00:06:58.085
much of the expansion.

00:06:58.725 --> 00:07:02.565
The size of the effect is therefore not a settled public number in every forum.

00:07:03.265 --> 00:07:08.085
What did not arrive was a comprehensive federal program reversing the land use changes attributed

00:07:08.085 --> 00:07:09.785
to the renewable fuel standard.

00:07:10.305 --> 00:07:14.485
Some states have tightened nutrient management rules for watersheds draining to the Gulf.

00:07:15.085 --> 00:07:19.185
The federal biofuel requirements continue to shape planting decisions each spring.

00:07:19.825 --> 00:07:25.325
Estimates of current nitrate loads still reflect the elevated baseline established after 2007.

00:07:25.905 --> 00:07:29.145
The persistence of the mandates reflects the statutory structure.

00:07:29.805 --> 00:07:36.025
Once the volume schedule is written into law, only new legislation or a successful lawsuit can change the core requirement.

00:07:36.665 --> 00:07:41.885
Later environmental programs have had to operate around an agricultural baseline that has already shifted.

00:07:42.929 --> 00:07:48.149
Hypoxia reduction work, in other words, inherited a farm map the fuel law had already redrawn.

00:07:48.149 --> 00:07:53.949
on. A state rule on how fertilizer is applied can matter. A state rule cannot, by itself,

00:07:54.229 --> 00:07:59.529
erase a federal reason to plant more corn. When Congress tied renewable fuel volumes directly

00:07:59.529 --> 00:08:05.649
to cornstarch ethanol in the 2007 act, the price premium on corn rewarded any farmer who

00:08:05.649 --> 00:08:11.829
could plant more of it. The reward did not depend on downstream nitrogen consequences. The EPA's

00:08:11.829 --> 00:08:17.529
annual blending obligations then transmitted that price signal year after year. Those obligations

00:08:17.529 --> 00:08:20.789
positions carried no automatic adjustment for water quality outcomes.

00:08:21.309 --> 00:08:25.749
Later attempts to meet hypoxia reduction goals therefore had to work against an agricultural

00:08:25.749 --> 00:08:28.749
system already reoriented by the earlier mandate.

00:08:29.469 --> 00:08:30.729
The mechanism is specific.

00:08:31.249 --> 00:08:32.589
The thing counted was gallons.

00:08:33.229 --> 00:08:37.769
The thing not counted inside that same compliance metric was nitrogen leaving the field.

00:08:38.269 --> 00:08:42.949
A metric that pays for volume will keep paying for volume after the river has already registered

00:08:42.949 --> 00:08:43.449
the cost.

00:08:43.449 --> 00:08:48.309
policy makers today weighing new fuel or feedstock targets can examine whether

00:08:48.309 --> 00:08:52.409
the compliance metric itself creates measurable pressure on land use or

00:08:52.409 --> 00:08:56.589
nutrient cycles before the volumes are locked into statute. If you want the

00:08:56.589 --> 00:09:01.089
longer watch on how rules meet watersheds, environmental intelligence on this

00:09:01.089 --> 00:09:05.469
network follows that pressure after the statute is already law. What would you

00:09:05.469 --> 00:09:10.169
watch for in a fuel or feedstock target now being drafted if the only number

00:09:10.169 --> 00:09:15.009
the statute is built to hit cannot see the river. We'll leave it there for today, thanks

00:09:15.009 --> 00:09:19.209
for thinking through this one with me. If you know someone who loves a good cautionary

